    "updated_at": "2023-08-24T18:45:21Z",
    "body": "Some apps that works with text (Microsoft Word, Notion) do have a distintion in the UI of having a «main title» tag and all the headings in body are equivalents to `<hx>` tags starting with the 1 level onward. Perhaps a solution would be to standarize an element to behave like a in-body main title for the page (somewhat in spirit like the head-only `<title>` element). If a new element is not feasible, it could be an `<h1>` tag with some special attribute that distinguishes it from the other headings.",
